# Contributing to the Flood Tool

## Style Guide

When contributing to the Flood Tool project, please adhere to the following style guidelines to ensure consistency and readability across the codebase:

- Follow PEP 8 naming conventions for variables and functions.
- Use docstrings to document all public classes and methods.
- Write unit tests for any new features or bug fixes.

## Pull Requests

When submitting a pull request, please ensure that:

- Your code passes all existing tests.
- You have added tests for any new functionality.
- You provide a clear description of the changes made and the reasons for them.
